      "content": "Endocrine System – Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Endocrine glands are ductless glands that secrete hormones directly into the bloodstream.",
        "The Pituitary Gland is located at the base of the brain and regulates the functioning of other endocrine glands.",
        "Thyroid gland produces Thyroxine, requiring iodine to maintain the basal metabolic rate (BMR).",
        "Insulin is secreted by the Beta cells of Islets of Langerhans in the pancreas to lower blood sugar levels.",
        "Adrenal glands secrete Adrenaline, preparing the body for emergency situations."
      ],
